WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.880
April 8th 16:00

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.380
Principal, you've got a message from
the Maritime Safety Support Department.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.590
Read it.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:15.600
Yes, ma'am. "If this Harekaze incident
can't be dealt with promptly within the school,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.680
it will be recognized as
a large-scale insurrection.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.600
In that case,
all of your school's ships will be seized.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.730
If that proves impossible, they will be sunk."

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.730
At this rate, it really will be deemed mutiny,

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.490
and the Blue Mermaid's main force may be
dispatched on a public security operation.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.280
We can't put our students in danger
when we don't even know the truth yet!

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.700
Let's try all possible means
for the sake of the students' safety.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.080
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.670
First, call the Director of the Ministry of Land,
Infrastructure, and Transportation.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.430
<i>An emergency distress call from the Musashi.</i>

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.180
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.610
Ms. Takeda.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.110
How is the main battery?

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.410
As you can see, we're inspecting it right now.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.200
It's automated for the most part,
but inspecting it is tough.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.750
Well, Hikari?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.830
This kid is still giving me grief.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.210
About how much longer will it take?

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.710
I'll get it done by sunset somehow.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.920
I appreciate it.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.050
Yep.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.850
We made some rice balls.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.600
- Thanks!
- It looks good!

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.470
The ones with faces have pickled plums inside.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.980
Ms. Matsunaga, Ms. Himeji,
are there any problems here?

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:14.860
- No problems with the launching tubes.
- Well, we don't even have a single torpedo.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.740
So you're having rice balls for lunch?

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.910
Everyone's too busy with repairs
to go to the dining hall.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.120
Is it true we got
an emergency distress call from the Musashi?

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.620
That's what I heard, too.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.290
I wonder what's going on
with the other ships.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.500
You're saying the whole world
has turned against us?!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.090
We can't let the Musashi sink!

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.670
Let's escape to the South Pole!

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.140
That's not a very funny idea.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.310
What?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.020
Damage Report

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.020
I've verified the damages.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.520
What's the situation?

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:56.520
At present, the engine is being repaired.
Battery number three is out of commission.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.570
We have no torpedoes.
We have one depth charge left.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.240
The tactical marine equipment
and surface radar are damaged.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.450
As for communications,
we can only receive messages.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:09.580
How long will it take if we place priority
repairing the necessities to be seaworthy?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.210
If it's only the engine,
we need another eight hours.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.090
We'll start there.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.460
Chief Engineer!

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.960
Can you repair it on the go?

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.630
<i>We can make it work! But we can't go
any faster than cruising speed!</i>

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.720
Understood.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.600
At cruising speed, we'll take
the shortest course back to school, Captain?

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:29.060
Captain?

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:30.850
Captain!

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.600
Shiro, what is it?

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.440
Please get your act together.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.150
Sorry, I was just...

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.330
Maritime Safety Support Department...

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.130
Apparently Ms. Yagi
intercepted an emergency message.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.170
- From where?
- From where?

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.340
It was an area-wide message
from the Maritime Safety Support Department.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.960
Area-wide message?

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:08.100
Let's see, "Currently, a Yokosuka Girls'
Marine High School ship has turned renegade.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.680
No ships from that high school
shall be allowed to stop at a port.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:17.810
Also, if the following ship offers any resistance,
it may be sunk without any repercussions:

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.820
the Destroyer, Harekaze"?!

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.570
S-Sunk?

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.610
I like firing,
but I hate being fired at!

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.870
Does that mean we can't stop at any port?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.740
It looks like it.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:34.080
W-we've totally become fugitives!

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.210
The Musashi may be in the same situation.
That's why the distress call...

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.090
Unlike us, that ship can't be sunk easily.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:48.390
- But they were asking for help. So—
- We're the ones who need help!

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:52.220
And how can we help anyone when we haven't
even done any practical skill exercises?

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.350
We shouldn't change our plan
to return to school.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.230
Let's report the Musashi to the school
and let them handle it.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:04.650
I understand. Just as Shiro says,
let's return to school.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.400
Aye.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.990
Okay, I'll be on the bridge,
so the rest of you can get some sleep.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.790
Rin and I are on duty tonight.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.750
You need to sleep too
in order to command properly.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.370
I'll be fine.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.380
Just get some sleep, please!

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.800
O-Okay. Understood, Shiro.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.260
<i>Moka.</i>

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:38.230
<i>I want to go help you. But right now...</i>

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.030
I have to start acting like a captain.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:03.250
<i>Captain. The sonar technician, Ms. Marikouji,
said she heard a strange noise underwater.</i>

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.550
<i>Captain! Captain!</i>

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:07.880
All hands to your station!

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.010
Coco, please report!

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:21.060
Um, there are two propellers 3,000 m away.
Currently conducting a sound analysis.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.230
There's nothing on the surface, so...

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:25.820
...a submarine?

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.950
What's up at a time like this?

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.240
Shiro, what's that?

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.910
What are you doing?

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:41.750
This is, um... Don't look!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.500
Main battery, ready!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.880
We're still fixing the engine.
We can't go any faster than cruising speed!

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.720
All clear from the watch!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.010
As far as I can see.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.430
A-All hands are at their stations.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:03.150
<i>Sound analysis completed.
It's I-201, a ship from Toumai High.</i>

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:04.730
Thank you, Ms. Marikouji.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.940
<i>You're welcome.</i>

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:07.440
Toumai High?

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.360
That's a boys' high school.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.950
Huh, a boys' school.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.910
Submarines are always from the boys' schools.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.870
But they're so cramped and hot and stinky.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.210
I-I can't deal with that!

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.750
They're obviously pursuing us.
Let's fire at them!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.130
Coco, can we get in contact with I-201?

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:33.260
Seawater will damp normal radio waves,
so we wouldn't reach them.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.010
So how do they normally contact each other?

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:39.140
Just because it's a submarine,
doesn't mean they're always underwater.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.150
Yeah, it would be scary if they didn't
check the surface once in a while.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:50.030
Shiro, when underwater, they're also using
sonar to see what's on the topside, right?

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:50.780
Of course.

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:54.910
Then why don't we use
our active sonar for Morse code?

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.530
I believe that would work.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:00.450
If we do that, they'll think we attacked them!

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.460
- Let's fire sonar or whatever at them!
- Don't talk nonsense!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.790
Ms. Marikouji, tell them our school, ship name,
and we have no intention of fighting.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.050
Received, and understood.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.890
Target has changed its depth.
It's suddenly diving deeper.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.770
What did I tell you?

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.650
But what if we could convey
our circumstances.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.240
That might be true, but we're fugitives!

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.200
See, they're pursuing us.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.950
L-Let's just get out of here!

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.460
Rin, slow ahead, at a speed
that doesn't interfere with the sonar.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.830
S-Slow ahead!

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.590
I wonder what kind of ship the I-201 is.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.050
Feature: History of Underwater High Speed Submarines

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.970
Let's see. Here it is.

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.560
Standard water displacement 1,070 tons.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.230
It's a fast ship that can move
at 20 knots underwater.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:11.360
Twenty knots is really slow
compared to the Harekaze.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:16.070
We're on the surface. If they can
go that fast underwater, it's incredible.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.950
Most submarines
can only move about six knots.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.330
Twenty and six.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.410
Wow, so it's about three times as fast.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:25.580
And their arms?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.210
Four 53 cm torpedo tubes, two 25 mm
single-mounted machine guns,

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.460
and ten torpedoes!

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.590
Two torpedoes heading our way!

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:36.260
Maron! Battle speed,
as much as you can give us!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.640
I've got my hands full right now.
Kuro, you do it!

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:40.680
Roger.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.390
Ms. Marikouji.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.310
<i>Where is the firing sound coming from?</i>

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:48.690
Both are coming from 27 degrees.
They're getting closer.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:49.900
3,000... 2,000.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.190
Roger.

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:00.160
Two torpedoes, 20 degrees off the port bow.
Approaching!

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.870
Rin! Hard left rudder!

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:04.240
Hard left rudder!

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.830
We escaped the torpedoes' collision course!

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.960
Two explosions off the ship's stern!

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.220
Eight torpedoes left.
Tama, prepare for artillery battle, port side!

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.800
<i>I can't see the target!</i>

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:26.730
- If we fire, they'll definitely treat us as hostile!
- I know! But for us to escape...

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:30.730
W-We could lose them if we go full spee—

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.650
<i>We can't go full speed!</i>

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.480
I-I know!

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.780
Ms. Marikouji, do you know their position?

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:41.030
I apologize,
but we would have to move more slowly.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.530
If we slow down, they'll sink us!

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.870
For now, let's just keep running around.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.800
<i>I don't see anything in the area.</i>

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:03.720
It's been an hour. With the speed difference,
I hope we've put enough distance between us.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:04.800
Really?

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:08.310
They can't stay underwater
at their max speed forever.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.940
Then maybe we managed to escape.

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:12.850
If it's escaping, leave it to me.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:15.270
Is that something to brag about?

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.230
C-Coco!

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.490
This worries me, Chief Navigator.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:30.080
<i>Ms. Marikouji, can you hear anything?</i>

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.330
Oh, I beg your pardon. I'm up now.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.710
Sorry to make you work this late.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.670
<i>Please hang in there a little longer.</i>

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.170
Certainly.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.350
I'm sleepy.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.350
No good. I'm so sleepy.

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:54.980
I made special Kinesaki-style
red bean buns for everyone.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:06.700
Two torpedoes, 120 degrees off the port bow,
3000 meters. Approaching!

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.450
W-What the?!

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.040
Six left.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.960
They found us pretty quickly.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.090
<i>Who's doing a lousy job of steering this ship?</i>

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:19.590
<i>Who's the captain?</i>

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.470
Is this ship a collection of amateurs?!

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:25.050
We're in the middle of battling a submarine.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.470
I know that!

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:30.310
And it's night warfare,
so why are your lights on?

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:31.770
Turn off all the lights!

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:35.480
- I can't see anything!
- That's because you're not used to the dark!

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:38.190
Turn off the navigation light, too. Imbeciles!

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:44.070
But we might collide with another ship.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:47.530
What kind of idiot shows themselves in battle?

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.450
Hard left rudder!

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:53.870
H-Hard left rudder!
Left rudder, 20 degrees.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.620
Keep your ears wide open.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.290
<i>Understood.</i>

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.960
This should buy us some time.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:03.670
Who are you?

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.390
- I am Wil—
- The girl from the German ship!

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.060
You're awake!

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.140
The battle is more important right now.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.270
Prepare to counterattack immediately.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.020
When a submarine is involved, leave it to me!

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:20.770
Since Germany is home of the submarines!

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:23.990
Leave it to the Germans.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:25.610
- The Germans.
- The Yourmans?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.280
We'll start with a basic depth charge!

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.620
We just have one.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.780
Then we'll go with a standard
anti-submarine mortar!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.580
We don't have stuff like that.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.250
A Mark 32 anti-sub torpedo.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.710
What year is that from? I don't even know it!

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.630
Then what do you have?!

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.790
That's right. We don't have anything.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.420
That's why I want your advice.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.220
Don't you have anything
that moves underwater?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.720
Anything!

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.440
Ready the paravane!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.650
Ready the paravane!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:00.980
Is this the paravane?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.480
Hocchan, Acchan, help me out here!

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.690
Got it!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.400
- It's heavy!
- My arms!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:08.660
We can do it!

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:13.540
One torpedo, 150 degrees off the port bow,
2,000 meters. Approaching!

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.500
Rin, hard right rudder!

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.000
Hard right rudder!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.920
Hard right rudder, 20 degrees!

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.590
Five left.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:31.800
Keep turning us right, 180 degrees,
so we're facing them directly!

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.300
Roger!

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.230
How's the paravane?

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.810
Mimi, are you okay?

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:46.780
- We have to stop it somehow.
- But the ship is swaying.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.070
Release the paravane!

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.250
That was close.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.830
Paravane ready!

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.460
Will that actually do anything?

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.500
Maybe.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.920
Engine room, can you give us
just one moment of top speed?

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.550
That's what she's requesting.

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.050
All right, just ten seconds!

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:15.680
Any more than that
and I'm not responsible!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.390
<i>Is what she said.</i>

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:18.220
Please!

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.180
<i>Alright!</i>

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:29.990
Did it just hit something?

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:30.950
I don't know.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:34.530
Should we try dropping our speed a bit?

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.700
No, this is where you lead them in.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.160
That was definitely them.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:41.290
You're sure?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.830
Okay. Got it.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:44.540
Rin, red 15.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.040
Red 15.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.670
Steadily drop speed until we get to high speed.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:51.220
Steady as she goes!

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.550
Tama, prepare for artillery battle!

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:53.430
Aye!

00:16:58.350 --> 00:16:59.680
<i>Sonar is picking up torpedoes!</i>

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:02.940
Four of them. Right behind us.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:04.230
Right rudder!

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.230
Right rudder!

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.690
Turn on the searchlight!

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:10.780
I found them!

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.530
Hard right rudder!

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.280
Battle! Starboard side artillery!

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.120
Fire!

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:29.250
Periscope sighted!
Starboard 10 degrees, two of them!

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:31.460
We're finally firing!

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:32.760
Throw down a depth charge!

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:33.840
Dropping a depth charge!

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:38.220
Right rudder!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.060
Steady as she goes!

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.490
<i>Air bubbles
off the starboard bow confirmed!</i>

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.740
<i>It's surfacing!</i>

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.240
Now! Let's escape, Captain!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.330
The shortest course is already set!

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:05.210
Cut the wire! High speed ahead!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:09.460
I-201's international distress call
and response confirmed.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:13.760
An instructor ship from Toumai High
is on its way at 30 knots.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:17.220
Hard left rudder!
30 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.850
Let's just get out of here!

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:34.360
April 9th 5:40

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:37.240
Ms. Minami, are you awake?

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:40.620
In spring, one sleeps like a log.

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.620
The sound of gunfire overnight.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.250
One enjoys a cup of tea.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:48.330
Thank you!

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:51.380
It's salty!

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.130
Blue Mermaid specialty, salty cocoa.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.380
Did you put salt in it, without any sugar?

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.850
Ms. Minami, was that on purpose?

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.140
Oh, where's the girl from the Spee?

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:07.140
What? You have business with me?

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:10.520
Thank you for before.
Your guidance saved us.

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.900
Well, I was jostled awake from my sleep.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.610
Can I ask you a question?

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.700
What happened on your ship?

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:23.280
Our ship, the Admiral Spee?

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:27.160
Yes. But if you don't want to talk about it...

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:32.790
I don't know all the details,
but I would like you to know.

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:38.880
Did you know our ship planned to participate
in the training exercises with your school?

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:41.260
No, this is the first I've heard.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.930
Well, that's ok.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:46.140
We were heading for the rendezvous point

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:49.810
but our electronics suddenly stopped working,
so when I went to investigate,

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:52.230
everyone stopped obeying orders.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:54.440
Mutiny?

00:19:56.230 --> 00:20:02.030
I don't know. The captain ordered me
to tell other ships, so I escaped.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.200
The captain?

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:06.580
I appreciate you picking up the cap, too.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:10.290
The captain entrusted me with it,
so it's very important.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.090
I must go back to the Spee
and return it to the captain.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:15.460
I swear.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.920
Got it. I'll help you.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.930
"One boat will be the savior."

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:31.560
When two strangers find themselves
in the same boat, they become unlikely allies.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:37.440
<i>Captain! The principal has ordered
all ships to return to port!</i>

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:43.070
Um, "I will not abandon any of our students.

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:49.750
For your protection too,
all ships return to school as soon as possible."

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:56.090
The school has ordered
all ships to return to port.

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:59.460
The school will assume responsibility
and protect the Harekaze too,

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.380
so they told us to come back.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:05.100
Also, all of the returning school's ships
are forbidden from engaging in battle.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:06.720
Thank goodness!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:10.850
However, there's still an alert out
for the Harekaze in the area.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:12.980
We can't stop at any port.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.230
We have to get back to school secretly.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:19.480
Also, I'd like to introduce you to a new friend.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:23.990
She's from Germany's
Winner Brown Sugar... Ingenmar...

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:25.870
What was it again?

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:26.700
Scheisse!

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.080
I'm from Wilhelmshaven High School.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:34.790
My name is Wilhelmina
Braunschweig Ingelner Friedeburg.

00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:37.920
I was the deputy-captain
for the Admiral Spee.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.170
That's long, so can we call you "Mi"?

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:41.590
Who the hell is "Mi"?

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.130
As for your room...

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.550
Which room is open, Coco?

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:49.720
Only the deputy-captain's room
has a spare bed.

00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:53.980
My room?

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.030
Wow, amazing.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.490
There's the shark from this evening.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:09.490
I never imagined Ms. Munetani's room
would be like this.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.080
It's a nice room.

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:16.000
I look forward to being your roomie.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:25.010
Episode 3: In a Pinch in Pajamas!
